1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,053
In 1946, ads told America:

2
00:00:03,053 --> 00:00:05,454
more doctors smoke this cigarette than any other.

3
00:00:05,454 --> 00:00:06,650
The proof?

4
00:00:06,650 --> 00:00:12,690
The ads claimed a survey of 113,597 doctors.

5
00:00:12,690 --> 00:00:13,816
But who ran it?

6
00:00:13,816 --> 00:00:15,534
Not scientists.

7
00:00:15,534 --> 00:00:17,806
The cigarette company's own ad agency.

8
00:00:17,806 --> 00:00:19,164
Its people showed up at medical

9
00:00:19,164 --> 00:00:21,126
conventions and doctors' offices.

10
00:00:21,126 --> 00:00:23,005
First, they handed out free cartons.

11
00:00:23,005 --> 00:00:24,630
Then they asked:

12
00:00:24,630 --> 00:00:26,952
so... which brand do you smoke?

13
00:00:26,952 --> 00:00:28,543
And medical journals?

14
00:00:28,543 --> 00:00:30,606
They were taking cigarette ad money too.

15
00:00:30,606 --> 00:00:32,731
Even JAMA, the doctors' own journal,

16
00:00:32,731 --> 00:00:34,646
only stopped in 1953.

17
00:00:34,646 --> 00:00:36,271
The doctors weren't selling cigarettes.

18
00:00:36,271 --> 00:00:37,140
The money was.
